<title>SINGAPORE: Acer Computer raises stake in Japan unit.</title>
<headline>Acer Computer raises stake in Japan unit.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Computer distributor Acer Computer International Ltd (ACI) said on Friday it had increased its stake in Japanese subsidiary Acer Japan Corporation (AJC) to 99.8 percent from 99.22 percent.</p>
<p>ACI, a unit of Taiwan's Acer Inc, said in a statement it had subscribed for 9,480 new shares in AJC for 474 million yen or about US$3.8 million.</p>
<p>AJC's paid-up capital is now 634.1 million yen from 160.1 million yen previously.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
